    "updated_at": "2022-02-28T13:00:34Z",
    "body": "> Should this be `allow-custom-protocols-top-navigation`? (In an ideal world \"top\" is redundant, but I'm not sure we're quite there yet with `registerProtocolHandler()`.)\r\n\r\nHappy to edit this PR if you, or someone else, think this is better. I was slightly reluctant, because this is handed off externally, so this is not really a main frame nor a subframe navigation.\r\n\r\nIf we do, can we start with the `allow-top-navigation-` prefix? This way, it would share a common prefix with two other sandbox flags. Maybe:\r\n- `allow-top-navigation-to-custom-scheme`\r\n- `allow-top-navigation-to-external-application`\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
